        "timestamp": 1785251375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14004#discussion_r3666721032\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This seems like a bandaid to me: it papers over the fact that the defining inst in the <code>mem_values</code> may be a removed instruction by just skipping the processing. Could we instead avoid inserting into <code>mem_values</code> if we determine the store is dead?</p>\n</blockquote>",
